{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>פרי צדיק</b> — the fruit of the thoughts of his intellect, to teach them discipline from his mouth, like the fruit of the tree of life." "<b>ולוקח</b> — from the matter of כי לקח טוב (Proverbs 4:2). And he explained: ומחכים נפשות — a wise man makes wise, and makes known to them the disciplines, like מה יקחך לבך יחכימך (Job 15:12). Another interpretation: acquires (קונה), like those who bring merchandise. And in the language of the Sages they call an acquisition מקח, that is, he acquires souls like slaves and maidservants, as in the matter of ועבד אויל (Proverbs 11:29)." "Another interpretation: ולוקח נפשות — with his wisdom he saves him from evil."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra quotes himself (the verse's own continued phrasing) and the parallel verse without explicit attribution; rendered as transmitted."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:18.659130871Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}